{"body":"## Result and exact scope\n\nBoth original assertions remain **unsolved, 5/5 substantive author turns**: the one-third diagonal half-reach question and the full asymmetric integer-k implication for the mono-constrained function phi. Only the A-to-B and B-to-C degree conditions are assumed, and distinct reached vertices are counted. The adjacent psi-symmetry problem in PR364 is separate.\n\nThe packet proves exact complete-uniform template values; a weighted rank-two incidence theorem; maximal-type inequalities; the symmetric threshold for equally weighted first parts with |A| <= 5k; and the full asymmetric implication for disjoint maximal neighborhoods, including laminar families, without a size bound. Quantitative deletion stability and explicit failed-cover/uncrossing mechanisms retain their exact restrictions. No arbitrary-size support reduction, universal laminarization or original counterexample is claimed.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Full independent AI-assisted source/proof audit: scoped PASS with no mandatory correction\n- 12,967,236 author assertions replay exactly; 30,053 separately written independent controls\n- All 39 frozen author files and five bound review files preserved exactly\n- Known primary bounds, finite LP duality and the weighted framework credited; no historical novelty certification or human peer-review claim\n\nStart at [PUBLICATION_STATUS.md](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/967e8e489aa4599f712d5ddcde62e591827f7e38/unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30004047/PUBLICATION_STATUS.md), then the five proofs and full review. OpenAI tools assisted research, proof drafting, verification and review.\n\n## Changes\n\nFresh-main integration preserves the final author checkpoint as second parent. Only 48 target artifacts and this target’s QUEUE status/turn cells change. Raw PDFs, images and imported records are excluded. Draft only; no merge or release requested.","headRefName":"math/30004047-two-step-density-reviewed","headRefOid":"5f576c1b527f88730c7ee15fd204536069753f9a","isDraft":true,"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/383"}
